 as an upp…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/scratch/sw; git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Outline.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"κσ̄/√n is judged as an upper end (\\\"holds\\\" = measured gap ≤ predicted in ≥ 90% of cells, with the between-pool interval).\",\n\"κσ̄/√n is judged as an upper end (\\\"holds\\\" = measured gap ≤ predicted in ≥ 90% of cells, with the between-pool interval). **Wording rule (added after idea-review of v3):** the delivered result states which term set the tolerance (0.005, the SE term, or 25%). \\\"Tracks\\\" is written only when the 25% or 0.005 term sets it and the slope CI excludes 0; when the SE term sets the tolerance, or the slope CI contains both 0 and 1, the outcome is worded \\\"consistent with the predictor, not discriminating\\\".\")\nrep(\"(ii) real configurations in the densest 0.02-wide window of full-pool accuracy (window chosen by count; dropped, and said so, if < 20 configurations).\",\n\"(ii) real configurations in the densest 0.02-wide window of full-pool accuracy (window chosen by count; dropped, and said so, if < 20 configurations). **(ii) is a near-null, not a null** (true θ can differ by up to 0.02, within test power at n = 240): the \\\"above nominal\\\" (nominal + 1 pp) judgement is made on (i) only; (ii) is reported as near-null with the pool-accuracy spread in the window beside each rate, and no \\\"above nominal\\\" is read from it.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit commit -qam \"Outline: C2 wording rule, C4 (ii) near-null (idea-review v3)\"; git push -q origin HEAD:main && git push -q origin HEAD:master; git log -1 --oneline\ncd /hutian/repo; forge issue comment 4 -b \"Both taken in Outline §2.2: C2 delivered result names the tolerance term and is worded 'consistent with, not discriminating' when the SE term sets it or the slope CI contains 0 and 1; C4 'above nominal' judged on (i) only, (ii) reported as near-null with the window's accuracy spread.\" | tail -1; forge issue close 4\nforge issue comment 4 -R world/experiment-repo -b \"FYI outline §2.2 additions (idea-review v3): C2 wording rule — state which tolerance term set it; C4 null (ii) is near-null: report window's pool-accuracy spread beside each rate, 'above nominal' judged on synthetic (i) only.\" | tail -1"]], "output": "```console\n4feb80b Outline: C2 wording rule, C4 (ii) near-null (idea-review v3)\nhttp://172.17.0.1:43275/world/story-repo/issues/4#issuecomment-43\nClosed #4\nhttp://172.17.0.1:43275/world/experiment-repo/issues/4#issuecomment-45\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "d028a979-d6db-5d17-8120-53259f6b60b0", "at": 1795649874.544753, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19545, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "7fa3bc8ce328f6698b88b6d92cfed3bf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "8fa3fa31-95d2-5124-b261-ca883451db04", "at": 1795649874.550122, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19546, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "7fa3bc8ce328f6698b88b6d92cfed3bf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "1bac0d63-5e10-51c7-a3d0-3c15972a4515", "at": 1795649874.5541532, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19547, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "7fa3bc8ce328f6698b88b6d92cfed3bf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "contex