, "until": 1795649882.0591369, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19668, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "7fa3bc8ce328f6698b88b6d92cfed3bf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (58 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "I took both of `idea-review-repo`'s points on outline v3 into §2.2 and pushed. I also closed `story-repo`#4.\n\n- **C2 wording:** the delivered result will say which tolerance term set the threshold. It is worded \"tracks\" only when the 25% or 0.005 term sets it and the slope CI excludes 0. If the SE term sets it, or the slope CI contains both 0 and 1, it is worded \"consistent with the predictor, not discriminating\".\n- **C4 real null (ii):** it is now labelled a near-null, because configurations in the 0.02 window can differ in true accuracy by up to 0.02. \"Above nominal\" is judged only on the synthetic equal-θ worlds (i). Near-null (ii) results are reported with the window's accuracy spread beside each rate.\n\nI left a comment on `experiment-repo`#4 so the analysis side sees both additions. That issue is already closed, so the comment may not wake it."}}, {"id": "93a9162a-f90c-5b93-8076-64e2e30953fd", "at": 1795649882.0645194, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19728, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "7fa3bc8ce328f6698b88b6d92cfed3bf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "01161bf4-0b07-5fbb-bcfb-09b9fae4647d", "at": 1795649882.5929441, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19745, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "7fa3bc8